{"item_id":"feed:/resources/materials/physical-vapor-deposition/","version_id":"fcf9079ad45657e09903d78c29d7b8ae301b4348d9c2d777777b5d1e831378a0","decision":"reject","reason":"The dated passage is a general manufacturing explainer about thin-film coatings, not a development in frontier AI, CAD, 3D modeling, or intelligent physical systems. It supplies no model capability, geometry workflow, or verification evidence relevant to the publication's lead topics.","piece_ids":[]}
{"item_id":"feed:/resources/materials/recrystallization-of-metals/","version_id":"ded55799bfd57b9e786dbfccb038115b95d469ba2c6a470457c0869c6e17bd6c","decision":"reject","reason":"This recent but general metallurgy reference explains recrystallization rather than reporting a relevant AI, CAD, or robotics development. It contains no checkable evidence about a frontier-model capability, design workflow, or physical-system verification.","piece_ids":[]}
{"item_id":"feed:/resources/supply-chain/oil-refinery/","version_id":"03628944819a5390db2f0c3005cb2bcb336118528a4d5c646d7dfe25c82500ea","decision":"reject","reason":"The item is a general guide to refinery processes and is outside the publication's AI-for-3D-modeling, CAD, and physical-systems scope. Its dated technical descriptions do not establish any relevant new capability or evidence for builders of those systems.","piece_ids":[]}
{"item_id":"feed:https://blog.cadalyst.com/cadmanagement/autodesk-university-2026-what-the-announcements-mean-for-cad-teams","version_id":"e991bf7bc957baf20c6e947cff7b9a0d159ef7a1b8b9d5f500f7e1c95d47573b","decision":"accept","reason":"This is fresh practitioner-oriented CAD coverage with a timestamped account of Autodesk University demonstrations and a useful separation of shipped features, beta or Tech Preview work, and longer-term plans. Its evidence supports that Autodesk presented connected CAD and agentic-PLM workflows, not that those workflows are production-proven: the motor-substitution and lawn-mower examples were live demonstrations under unstated conditions. It adds commercial perspective, while independent evaluation and working-engineer evidence remain missing.","piece_ids":["01","03"]}
{"item_id":"feed:https://cableteque.com/blog/build-bom-from-wire-harness-drawing","version_id":"1eafb0dcff5f6f5b8c341b6abe613a9a77ce26e7c0fc4eef73af6790f2ae7fe5","decision":"defer","reason":"The timestamped description is relevant because it claims to turn drawing packages into structured wire-harness BOMs and flag compatibility gaps, but the claimed performance is vendor-reported. The cited KCM Cable result gives a workload and elapsed times, yet supplies no source drawings, extraction accuracy, exception rate, review protocol, or independent replication. Its claims also overlap the other Cableteque items from the same publisher and therefore do not independently corroborate them.","piece_ids":[]}
{"item_id":"feed:https://cableteque.com/blog/does-cableteque-quote-extract-boms-automatically-from-customer-pdf-drawings","version_id":"6d917d47e8d4b52b9fe4f0290327adf5dea0f67fa26266abe25051ad74adc0af","decision":"defer","reason":"PDF-to-BOM extraction is relevant to CAD-adjacent engineering workflows, and the item is dated, but its up-to-96% time-saving and two-minute claims are Cableteque's own claims without disclosed datasets, attempt counts, accuracy measures, or independently inspectable graders. The text instructs users to manually check extracted items, which is useful context but does not validate the automation's reliability. It repeats the same underlying Cableteque product claims found in the other company posts, not independent evidence.","piece_ids":[]}
{"item_id":"feed:https://cableteque.com/blog/losing-money-on-cable-assembly-quotes","version_id":"33abdbe4f75624efed189d40297ade0c2f12f250f578435d87954b3c34d4693e","decision":"defer","reason":"The item identifies a relevant engineering problem—unstructured drawings and omitted components causing quoting errors—but presents the platform's extraction, compatibility, pricing, and labor-fill claims as vendor assertions. The Resco turnaround anecdote lacks source packages, baseline definitions, accuracy checks, and independent observation, so it cannot establish the claimed capability. It is also same-publisher coverage of the same underlying Cableteque workflow, not corroboration.","piece_ids":[]}
{"item_id":"feed:https://cableteque.com/blog/retiring-estimator-quoting-knowledge","version_id":"7684d3f81b48f399e04d30dd15d5c9125d3b3466ed41c07228ed6dc7b4631cc7","decision":"defer","reason":"Capturing compatibility and labor knowledge from experienced estimators is relevant to engineering automation, but the article's product claims are not checked beyond Cableteque's account. Its survey size, parts-library assertions, automation percentages, and Derrick Lang outcome lack methodology, underlying records, or independently reproducible evaluation. These are repeated same-publisher claims about the same product and should not be treated as independent support.","piece_ids":[]}
{"item_id":"feed:https://cableteque.com/news/ai-wire-harness-quoting-europe","version_id":"3f0b6128cabb2c363faca5fff7b5511c50c36083101892f525858da4428f081b","decision":"accept","reason":"This dated company announcement is relevant startup context: Cableteque reports a European launch, Europe Central data hosting beginning September 30, and planned—not completed—ISO 27001 certification for December. It is credible only for what the company says it is launching and planning; the release offers no independent check that its extraction, quoting, or engineering claims work in European deployments. Treat it as a commercial availability and governance signal, not technology-performance evidence.","piece_ids":["01","03"]}
{"item_id":"feed:https://mit-cdfg.github.io/Survey-AI-for-3D-modeling-Robotics/#view-stats","version_id":"08b1c2cdebb5796d7332d57e8928784a621aec9f82db91448016eaa53ea51fe5","decision":"accept","reason":"This fresh research-oriented survey directly addresses frontier models for editable 3D scenes, parametric CAD, and robotics, and states its evidence scope: 1,646 public posts across 707 cases, with only 132 cases providing runnable code. Its strongest contribution is its explicit credibility boundary: benchmark and demonstration results support first-draft capability, while tolerances, manufacturability, withheld-condition transfer, and safe unsupervised operation remain untested or weakly tested. The compilation is not independent replication of every underlying claim, but it makes the distinction between evidence types and system harnesses explicit, providing a needed research perspective alongside commercial coverage.","piece_ids":["01","02","03"]}
